#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105483 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "62405619-31ca-5403-aa45-360e6b3fbd59" :question/math-academy-id "e-3289" :question/problem "Find the area of $\\triangle{ABC}$ below. Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/f15aebd48fba864b6b804273ece662d0.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A}=\\dfrac{1}{2}ab\\sin{C}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\angle{C}$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $b$.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na &= CB = 58 \\\\\nb &= CA = 40 \\\\\nm\\angle C &= 31^{\\circ }\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\sin{31^{\\circ}} = 0.515\\,038\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places, we calculate the area as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 58 \\cdot 40\\sin 31^{\\circ } \\\\\n&= 1160 \\cdot (0.515038) \\\\\n&\\approx 597.44\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105484 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/id #uuid "b41b2354-c339-5398-ab43-5886b8447c1c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3294" :question/problem "Rounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/df17bd0e04a4bf54f78403799e52df63.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle ADC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/43f655045f30483b6371dd630b70d121.png)\n\nFirst, we find the area for $\\triangle ABC$, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABC} &= \\frac{1}{2}(42)(35)\\sin 36^{\\circ } \\\\\n&= 735\\sin 36^{\\circ } \\\\\n&\\approx 432.022\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $\\triangle ADC$, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ADC} &= \\frac{1}{2}(20)(18)\\sin 80^{\\circ } \\\\\n&= 180\\sin 80^{\\circ } \\\\\n&\\approx 177.265\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABCD} &= A_{ABC} + A_{ADC} \\\\\n&= 432.022 + 177.265 \\\\\n&\\approx 609\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $609$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105485 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle Given the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/id #uuid "472216c8-da7d-58fb-9056-e71d5e33460d" :question/math-academy-id "e-3297" :question/problem "The area of $ABCD$ is $300\\, \\text{cm}^2$. What is the area of $\\triangle ABC$ rounded to the nearest integer?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/082daac33f9eacc4721718b0450a9b3d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $\\triangle ACD$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ACD} &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot DA \\cdot DC \\cdot \\sin D \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(25)(32)\\sin 70^{\\circ } \\\\\n&= 400\\sin 70^{\\circ } \\\\\n&= 375.877\\ldots \\\\\n&\\approx 376\\,\\mathrm{cm}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ and $\\triangle ACD$ gives the area of $\\triangle ABC$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{ABC} &= A_{ACD} - A_{ABCD} \\\\\n&= 376 - 300 \\\\\n&= 76\\,\\mathrm{cm}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105502 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "c8d31ea4-41c6-5f24-bf7a-a950a30342d7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4253" :question/problem "The area of ​​the triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is $24\\sqrt{2} \\text{cm}^2$. Find $AB$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/baf9217d37cc64a0caa8560240c0a729.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A}=\\dfrac{1}{2}bc\\sin{A}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\angle{A}$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c$.\n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nc &= AB, \\\\\nb &= AC = 12\\,\\mathrm{cm}, \\\\\nm\\angle A &= 45^{\\circ }\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\sin{45^{\\circ}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $c=AB$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot b \\cdot c \\cdot \\sin A \\\\\n24\\sqrt{2} &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 12 \\cdot c \\cdot \\sin 45^{\\circ } \\\\\n24\\sqrt{2} &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 12 \\cdot c \\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\\n24\\sqrt{2} &= 3\\sqrt{2}c \\\\\n24 &= 3c \\\\\nc &= 8\\,\\mathrm{cm}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\nAB = 8\\,\\textrm{cm}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80630a24-1a3a-5eff-9020-9923a9bed1e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102298} {:answer/id #uuid "a55a71eb-ac61-50c7-a583-f5285013ec99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102299} {:answer/id #uuid "c4794c8c-97f0-5a52-ae43-9bbaea86e6d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102300} {:answer/id #uuid "e30e9cca-33d8-5541-bb5b-43e9a560b683" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102301} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b595c0-f7a4-5417-93c9-502948f8db58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3b595c0-f7a4-5417-93c9-502948f8db58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102302} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd90ce6-9952-55a8-b467-0f715bd47248" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102297}] :question/id #uuid "306dd89a-2c53-58e5-b9e0-196c65483287" :question/math-academy-id "q-18021" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1275/Source/Images/q-18021.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC$. Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle Given the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae0bec27-87b5-5caf-9b22-0ecb9e031b5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102316} {:answer/id #uuid "b642c2ca-9d40-57b1-a77d-1a949817a88c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102317} {:answer/id #uuid "dbce89a8-29b3-5594-b5f6-bb1c1eedbf66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102318} {:answer/id #uuid "54c83ad9-ea17-52a2-b9d2-7f65419bfbbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102319} {:answer/id #uuid "560ca569-8895-59bc-920f-321a417a0d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38in^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102320}] :answer-fie